  "implementation": [
    "The ordinary ORDER resolver distinguishes a rowid-first cursor order from a source sorter. Rowid directions reuse actual source rows in forward/reverse order; a sorter executes through the actual read compiler before common accepted-point execution, retaining later target-failure effects.",
    "The shared register source interpreter retains actual DISTINCT values across source steps and OFFSET. Duplicate decisions use the existing collation-aware equality; actual earlier writes affect later source register reads.",
    "Source-free UNION ALL leaves become ordinary coroutine inputs without evaluating values early. Static WHERE leaves are admitted only from actual checked constant conditions; complete original preparation still validates disabled branches. Empty AUTOINCREMENT completion writes the real zero sequence entry.",
    "Physical-table subqueries reuse the existing projection inliner and real schema star expansion. Inlining retains actual source cursors/counter observations and leaves self-read, indexed and other source plans on their existing paths.",
    "ValuesInput evaluates the complete real VALUES row once, then passes those values through the ordinary lexical frame for its outer projection. The actual metadata compiler supplies column names/scopes. VALUES columns carry no expression affinity and clear subquery JSON subtype, as pinned native controls establish; no dummy input or query output is used.",
    "Explicit aggregate/window/capture and clause boundaries keep their dedicated plans. Generated source declarations validate before execution starts. The new VALUES producer currently admits plain UTF-8 projections without WHERE/group/order/DISTINCT or row windows. The native shim remains unchanged."
  ],
  "evaluation_protocols": {
    "public_file_modes": "7246 stdout/exit/first-error and independent persisted catalog/row/integrity comparisons in rollback/WAL modes, including 90 new register-plan cases.",
    "same_connection": "167 state-carrying Core API comparisons versus the pinned non-bailing shell; fresh final generated input cases and fixed native controls are separate from file comparisons.",
    "select_input_regressions": "All 12 independently selectable regressions now pass normally; they remain an independent metric and are not added to the 167 API or 7246 file totals.",
    "named_features": "Eight failures in the separate 88-case named feature survey remain; no survey defines a global compatibility percentage."
  },
  "proof_scope": "All retained contracts and audits compile. The register loop retains its existing LIMIT-zero law over the shared interpreter. A new audited component law keeps the VALUES producer outside unsupported database encodings. The maintained executable group checks rowid ordering, DISTINCT, sorter observations, UNION yields, physical-source inlining, actual VALUES registers and native affinity/subtype boundaries. No complete SELECT/VDBE equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "The twelve maintained SELECT input regressions are fixed. Broader producer combinations, nontrivial indexed/captured/compound/deferred plans and full SQL equivalence remain work.",
    "Wider error codes/phases, FAIL/IGNORE/ROLLBACK controls, triggered UPSERT, INSTEAD OF/temp triggers, writable CTEs, trigger-aware ALTER and deferred private-function declarations remain work.",
    "Eight of 88 named probes still fail: WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys and partial/expression indexes, both modes. These probes do not define global coverage.",
    "UTF-16 writes/setters, native-key/materialization limits, pending new physical allocations and earlier SQL/storage limitations remain. The finite process-kill samples do not establish every syscall/power-loss schedule."
  ],
